1
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:05,668
Story title: Transforming Heart Disease Prediction Using Quantum Enhanced Technology, Nature.

2
00:00:06,320 --> 00:00:12,484
Story Title: Quantum Leap in Heart Disease Prediction: A New Era of Quantum Enhanced Machine Learning.

3
00:00:13,166 --> 00:00:24,580
In the rapidly evolving world of artificial intelligence and machine learning, a groundbreaking study published in Scientific Reports has unveiled a revolutionary development that could redefine the future of heart disease prediction.

4
00:00:25,262 --> 00:00:39,588
The research, conducted by a team of experts in the field, has demonstrated the potential of quantum enhanced machine learning, QML, algorithms in accurately predicting heart disease, surpassing traditional machine learning approaches by a significant margin.

5
00:00:40,366 --> 00:00:53,700
The latest study, titled, Revolutionizing Heart Disease Prediction with Quantum Enhanced Machine Learning, highlights the power of QML in diagnosing complex health disorders, such as heart disease, by harnessing the capabilities of quantum technology.

6
00:00:54,414 --> 00:01:04,324
By integrating quantum computing principles into machine learning algorithms, the research showcases a promising approach for enhancing the accuracy and efficiency of heart disease prediction.

7
00:01:04,974 --> 00:01:15,140
The study evaluated the performance of QML against traditional machine learning algorithms using the Kaggle heart disease dataset, which contains 1,190 samples.

8
00:01:15,854 --> 00:01:21,572
The dataset was divided into 53% positive samples and 47% negative samples.

9
00:01:22,254 --> 00:01:30,916
The performance of QML was measured using metrics such as accuracy, precision, recall, specificity, F1 score, and training time.

10
00:01:31,598 --> 00:01:44,260
The results revealed that QML outperformed traditional machine learning approaches by predicting around 50.03% of positive samples as positive and an average of 44.65% of negative samples as negative.

11
00:01:44,974 --> 00:01:55,620
In contrast, traditional machine learning approaches could predict only around 49.78% of positive samples as positive and 44.31% of negative samples as negative.

12
00:01:56,302 --> 00:02:11,876
Moreover, QML consumed an average of 670 microseconds for its training, while traditional machine learning algorithms required an average of 862.5 microseconds, making QML a faster and more accurate approach in heart disease prediction.

13
00:02:12,590 --> 00:02:18,532
The study's findings are particularly significant as heart disease has emerged as a leading cause of human death worldwide.

14
00:02:19,246 --> 00:02:25,316
Changes in food habits, lifestyle, and work-related stress contribute to the increasing rate of heart disease.

15
00:02:25,998 --> 00:02:34,980
According to the World Health Organization, 17.7 million people suffer from heart disease each year, with coronary artery disease being the most common type.

16
00:02:35,758 --> 00:02:40,420
Early detection and intervention are crucial in reducing the mortality rate of heart disease.

17
00:02:41,102 --> 00:02:49,668
Traditional methods for diagnosing heart disease include manual examination of risk factors, physical examination reports, and analyzing patient symptoms.

18
00:02:50,350 --> 00:02:55,844
However, these methods can be inaccurate due to hidden parameters and high computational costs.

19
00:02:56,494 --> 00:03:02,884
Angiography, a precise method for diagnosing CAD, is associated with high costs and major side effects.

20
00:03:03,630 --> 00:03:07,908
Healthcare sectors are struggling to offer reliable diagnoses at a reasonable cost.

21
00:03:08,622 --> 00:03:14,000
Moreover, image-based detections are more costly and not suitable for screening large populations.

22
00:03:14,830 --> 00:03:22,980
In recent years, machine learning algorithms have shown promising results in terms of greater accuracy rate and speed in early diagnosis of heart disease.

23
00:03:23,694 --> 00:03:30,948
These algorithms can identify hidden patterns in large datasets, making them valuable tools for predicting complex health disorders.

24
00:03:31,630 --> 00:03:39,044
Despite the benefits, traditional machine learning algorithms face computational limitations when dealing with larger and more complex data.

25
00:03:39,694 --> 00:03:41,280
Enter Quantum Computing.

26
00:03:41,582 --> 00:03:52,452
Quantum-enhanced machine learning algorithms facilitate healthcare industries to evaluate and treat complicated health disorders by addressing the computational bottleneck of traditional machine learning algorithms.

27
00:03:53,166 --> 00:04:01,828
By integrating quantum computing and machine learning, QML enhances computational power, enabling faster and more accurate diagnosis of heart disease.

28
00:04:02,510 --> 00:04:09,764
The study's major contribution is conducting an experimental study on various machine learning algorithms used for heart disease prediction.

29
00:04:10,446 --> 00:04:19,780
The research identified suitable machine learning methods and evaluated the essentials of quantum computing integration to enhance machine learning algorithms' speed and accuracy.

30
00:04:20,462 --> 00:04:27,652
The proposed QML techniques were evaluated based on selected features, demonstrating greater accuracy and speed in prediction.

31
00:04:28,430 --> 00:04:33,284
The future of heart disease prediction lies in the synergy of machine learning and quantum computing.

32
00:04:34,030 --> 00:04:42,820
As the study reveals, QML holds the potential to revolutionize heart disease prediction, setting the stage for a new era of accurate and efficient diagnosis.

33
00:04:43,534 --> 00:04:54,564
With further research and development, QML could pave the way for a future where heart disease is detected and treated earlier and more effectively, ultimately improving the quality of life for millions of people worldwide.

34
00:04:55,214 --> 00:04:58,820
Source www.nature.com.

35
