Story title Quantum Enhanced Machine Learning Revolutionizes Heart Disease Prediction.

37
00:05:11,086 --> 00:05:20,356
In the modern world, heart disease has become a leading cause of human death, with changes in food habits, lifestyle, and work-related stress contributing to its increase.

38
00:05:21,006 --> 00:05:27,428
The World Health Organization states that 17.7 million people worldwide suffer from heart disease each year.

39
00:05:28,110 --> 00:05:37,668
According to a report released by the Global Burden of Disease in 2016, 1.7 million Indians were affected by cardiovascular diseases, CVD, 2.

40
00:05:38,382 --> 00:05:46,692
Coronary artery disease, CAD, is the most common type of CVD, caused by blockage or obstruction in at least one of the coronary arteries.

41
00:05:47,406 --> 00:05:54,692
Early detection of CAD is crucial for effective treatment, and machine learning algorithms have shown promising results in diagnosing heart disease.

42
00:05:55,342 --> 00:06:02,212
However, traditional machine learning algorithms struggle with larger and more complex data due to computational limitations.

43
00:06:02,894 --> 00:06:11,428
This is where quantum computing comes in, enhancing computational power and facilitating healthcare industries to evaluate and treat complicated health disorders.

44
00:06:12,110 --> 00:06:19,332
In a recent study, researchers conducted an experimental study of various machine learning algorithms used for heart disease prediction.

45
00:06:20,014 --> 00:06:28,708
From the study, suitable machine learning methods were identified, and the essentials of quantum computing integration to enhance machine learning algorithms were revealed.

46
00:06:29,390 --> 00:06:38,372
The proposed quantum enhanced machine learning QML, techniques were then evaluated based on selected features, showing greater accuracy and speed in prediction.

47
00:06:39,054 --> 00:06:53,508
The QML techniques were compared with traditional machine learning approaches, and the results demonstrated that QML outperformed traditional methods with an accuracy rate of 0.6% higher and a training time of 192.5 microseconds faster.

48
00:06:54,190 --> 00:07:01,284
This shows that QML is a promising approach in heart disease prediction, providing a more efficient and accurate method for early detection.

49
00:07:01,966 --> 00:07:10,596
The integration of quantum computing and machine learning is revolutionizing the healthcare industry, offering a faster and more reliable solution for heart disease prediction.

50
00:07:11,310 --> 00:07:20,804
As quantum computers become more accessible, QML techniques will significantly impact the healthcare sector, leading to improved patient outcomes and more efficient healthcare systems.

